1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,500
This train has two passengers without tickets. Right now they are pretending to be yarn.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,100
The night train hasn't left yet. Their breath almost left first.

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,700
Here, tickets cost acorns. The clerk counts the change in her cheeks.

4
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:10,300
They have a pebble, a map, fish skewers and a parcel. No acorns.

5
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,900
Two trains. Mochi checked his map and chose with confidence. That is the worrying part.

6
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,300
Then Kong noticed something. Parcels don't need tickets.

7
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,900
A delivery worker's trick. Mochi has no good memories of boxes.

8
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,300
Inside a box again. This time he is not alone.

9
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,500
Snowflake stamp, bang. Not passengers now, but cargo.

10
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:25,100
Cargo car reached. But why is that box in the corner moving on its own?

11
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,500
The Snowflake Train runs through the night. It only snows where it has passed.

12
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,100
The passenger car was warm. The bird on the ceiling is the train's navigation.

13
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,500
And then the conductor came. Click, click.

14
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,100
Hiding spot one: under the seat. The backpack refuses to cooperate.

15
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,700
Granny Sheep holds out her ticket. Right now, right in front of his face.

16
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:40,300
Hiding spot two: inside the yarn. Granny saw nothing at all.

17
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,700
The conductor finds the yarn suspicious. The yarn holds its breath.

18
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:45,300
Of all times, the snack cart rolls by. A snack on every spine.

19
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,700
Mochi's nose does not listen to its owner.

20
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,700
Their eyes met.

21
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:52,100
The ticketless passengers run down the aisle. So does the yarn.

22
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,300
The car ends here.

23
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:57,100
Kong shows the stamp on the parcel. Mochi offers the fish skewer from the diner.

24
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,700
Rules are rules. But the fish was still warm.

25
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:02,500
Click. A snowflake hole in the parcel. Now this is their ticket.

26
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:05,300
Proper passengers at last. But why does the bird keep pointing backward?

27
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:09,300
The first sun is up. The map was upside down, and the train is going the other way. (To be continued)

